er science; accept equivalent original wording."},{"type":"list","items":["Inputs, processing and outputs should be identified clearly.","The design should be tested using representative data.","Security and privacy should be considered from the start.","The chosen approach should be justified against relevant constraints.","Clear documentation makes a system easier to maintain.","The solution should meet the stated user need."]}],"marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Inputs, processing and outputs should be identified clearly.","marks":1},{"criteria":"The design should be tested using representative data.","marks":1},{"criteria":"Security and privacy should be considered from the start.","marks":1},{"criteria":"The chosen approach should be justified against relevant constraints.","marks":1},{"criteria":"Clear documentation makes a system easier to maintain.","marks":1},{"criteria":"The solution should meet the stated user need.","marks":1}],"model_answer":[{"type":"text","value":"A strong response applies these computer science ideas to the fictional organisation:"},{"type":"list","items":["Inputs, processing and outputs should be identified clearly.","The design should be tested using representative data.","Security and privacy should be considered from the start.","The chosen approach should be justified against relevant constraints.","Clear documentation makes a system easier to maintain.","The solution should meet the stated user need."]}]},"learning_guidance":{"hints":["For data exchange between the bike-hire devices, focus on computer science. Start from what the people using the system need it to achieve.","Connect the required result to its information, resources, checks and safeguards.","Weigh a benefit against a limitation for data exchange between the bike-hire devices, then decide which matters most to bike-hire staff. Support the conclusion with those reasons."],"model_answer":"Inputs, processing and outputs should be identified clearly. For data exchange between the bike-hire devices, this identifies what information enters the system, what it does with that information and what it returns.\\n\\nThe design should be tested using representative data. This checks that data exchange between the bike-hire devices works for the kinds of input it is expected to receive.\\n\\nSecurity and privacy should be considered from the start. This helps avoid exposing information or allowing unauthorised actions in data exchange between the bike-hire devices.\\n\\nThe chosen approach should be justified against relevant constraints. For data exchange between the bike-hire devices, this means balancing user requirements against resources such as time, budget and available equipment.\\n\\nClear documentation makes a system easier to maintain. This helps another person operate, repair or extend the system supporting data exchange between the bike-hire devices.\\n\\nThe solution should meet the stated user need. For data exchange between the bike-hire devices, the organisation should establish what its users must be able to do before selecting technology.\\n\\nA useful design can improve the service, but extra features may increase cost, maintenance and privacy risks without helping the main user need.\\n\\nFor data exchange between the bike-hire devices, I would start with the core user need, choose a proportionate design and test its function, security and maintainability before expanding it. This balances the needs of bike-hire staff against the limitations above."}},{"question_id":"6(b)(ii)","parent_question":6,"topic":"star topology diagram","marks":3,"command_word":"draw","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Harbour Arts Centre is planning a new online booking service. This is an original comp.school fixture scenario."},{"type":"text","value":"Explain how primary memory is relevant to this situation. Link each point to the needs of the organisation."}],"answer":{"guidance":[{"type":"text","value":"Award marks for accurate, relevant points about primary memory; accept equivalent original wording."},{"type":"list","items":["Accessing virtual memory is slower than accessing RAM.","Memory capacity is measured using units such as bytes, kilobytes and gigabytes.","RAM stores programs and data currently in use and is volatile."]}],"marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Accessing virtual memory is slower than accessing RAM.","marks":1},{"criteria":"Memory capacity is measured using units such as bytes, kilobytes and gigabytes.","marks":1},{"criteria":"RAM stores programs and data currently in use and is volatile.","marks":1}],"model_answer":[{"type":"text","value":"A strong response applies these primary memory ideas to the fictional organisation:"},{"type":"list","items":["Accessing virtual memory is slower than accessing RAM.","Memory capacity is measured using units such as bytes, kilobytes and gigabytes.","RAM stores programs and data currently in use and is volatile."]}]},"learning_guidance":{"hints":["For the online booking service, focus on primary memory. Think about what must be available while a device is running and what is needed when it starts.","Compare how long information must be kept with how quickly the running program needs it.","Link each technical point to an effect on the online booking service. Make the reason for that effect explicit, without assuming facts about the organisation that the scenario does not give."],"model_answer":"Accessing virtual memory is slower than accessing RAM. Frequent use of virtual memory can therefore delay the online booking service.\\n\\nMemory capacity is measured using units such as bytes, kilobytes and gigabytes. These units allow the organisation to compare the memory required by the online booking service with device capacity.\\n\\nRAM stores programs and data currently in use and is volatile. Data being used by the online booking service must also be saved to persistent storage if it is needed after shutdown."}},{"question_id":"6(c)","parent_question":6,"topic":"network security table","marks":6,"command_word":"complete","content":[{"type":"text","value":"A local games studio is testing a prototype made with invented data. This is an original comp.school fixture scenario."},{"type":"text","value":"Complete 4 accurate points about computer networks."}],"answer":{"guidance":[{"type":"text","value":"Award marks for accurate, relevant points about computer networks; accept equivalent original wording."},{"type":"list","items":["A wide area network connects devices across a larger geographical area.","A switch forwards frames to the intended device on a local network.","A router forwards packets between different networks.","Client-server networks centralise services and administration.","Network performance is affected by bandwidth, latency, traffic and transmission media.","A local area network connects devices across a limited geographical area."]}],"marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"A wide area network connects devices across a larger geographical area.","marks":1},{"criteria":"A switch forwards frames to the intended device on a local network.","marks":1},{"criteria":"A router forwards packets between different networks.","marks":1},{"criteria":"Client-server networks centralise services and administration.","marks":1},{"criteria":"Network performance is affected by bandwidth, latency, traffic and transmission media.","marks":1},{"criteria":"A local area network connects devices across a limited geographical area.","marks":1}],"model_answer":[{"type":"text","value":"A strong response applies these computer networks ideas to the fictional organisation:"},{"type":"list","items":["A wide area network connects devices across a larger geographical area.","A switch forwards frames to the intended device on a local network.","A router forwards packets between different networks.","Client-server networks centralise services and administration.","Network performance is affected by bandwidth, latency, traffic and transmission media.","A local area network connects devices across a limited geographical area."]}]},"learning_guidance":{"hints":["For testing the games prototype, focus on computer networks. Identify which devices or locations need to exchange information.","Distinguish the scale of the connection, the equipment carrying data and the way shared services are managed.","For each of your 4 points, explain why the property matters to testing the games prototype. Link related details where useful, and make the reason explicit rather than only naming a feature."],"model_answer":"- A local area network connects devices across a limited geographical area. This allows devices at one site to share resources used in testing the games prototype. A wide area network connects devices across a larger geographical area. This could connect the sites or remote services needed by testing the games prototype.\\n- A switch forwards frames to the intended device on a local network. This helps devices at the same site exchange data for testing the games prototype. A router forwards packets between different networks. This allows data for testing the games prototype to reach services outside the local network.\\n- Client-server networks centralise services and administration. This lets the organisation manage shared accounts and resources for testing the games prototype from a central service.\\n- Network performance is affected by bandwidth, latency, traffic and transmission media. The organisation must consider both connection capacity and delay when planning data exchange for testing the games prototype."}},{"question_id":"7(a)","parent_question":7,"topic":"defragmentation benefits","marks":3,"command_word":"explain","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Oakfield Food Co-op is modernising its stock-control system. This is an original comp.school fixture scenario."},{"type":"text","value":"Explain how systems software is relevant to this situation. Link each point to the needs of the organisation."}