ital services can improve access but may exclude people without suitable devices or connectivity.","Manufacturing and disposing of hardware has environmental costs.","Stakeholders can experience different benefits and drawbacks from the same technology."]}]},"learning_guidance":{"hints":["For the stock-control system, focus on impacts of digital technology. Identify the people affected by the proposed digital change.","Compare a possible improvement with a possible disadvantage for a different stakeholder or resource.","For each of your 4 points, explain why the property matters to the stock-control system. Link related details where useful, and make the reason explicit rather than only naming a feature."],"model_answer":"- Stakeholders can experience different benefits and drawbacks from the same technology. The organisation should consider users, staff and others affected by the stock-control system before choosing a solution. A justified decision weighs consequences, rights, costs and practical safeguards. The decision about the stock-control system should therefore balance useful improvements with its effects on people and resources.\\n- Personal data should be collected for a clear purpose and protected appropriately. The organisation should limit the information collected for the stock-control system to what it needs and control access to it.\\n- Automation can improve efficiency while changing the kinds of work people do. People involved in the stock-control system may need training or changes to their responsibilities as processes change. Digital services can improve access but may exclude people without suitable devices or connectivity. The organisation should consider an accessible alternative for people who cannot use the digital route to the stock-control system.\\n- Manufacturing and disposing of hardware has environmental costs. The organisation can reduce waste from the stock-control system by extending equipment life and using appropriate recycling."}},{"question_id":"11","parent_question":11,"topic":"smartphone upgrade impact","marks":8,"command_word":"discuss","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Riverside Wildlife Centre is updating its computing systems. This is an original comp.school fixture scenario."},{"type":"text","value":"Discuss how computer science should be used in this situation. Develop both benefits and limitations before reaching a justified conclusion."}],"answer":{"guidance":[{"type":"text","value":"Award marks for accurate, relevant points about computer science; accept equivalent original wording."},{"type":"list","items":["The design should be tested using representative data.","Security and privacy should be considered from the start.","The chosen approach should be justified against relevant constraints.","Clear documentation makes a system easier to maintain.","The solution should meet the stated user need.","Inputs, processing and outputs should be identified clearly."]}],"marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"The design should be tested using representative data.","marks":2},{"criteria":"Security and privacy should be considered from the start.","marks":2},{"criteria":"The chosen approach should be justified against relevant constraints.","marks":1},{"criteria":"Clear documentation makes a system easier to maintain.","marks":1},{"criteria":"The solution should meet the stated user need.","marks":1},{"criteria":"Inputs, processing and outputs should be identified clearly.","marks":1}],"model_answer":[{"type":"text","value":"A strong response applies these computer science ideas to the fictional organisation:"},{"type":"list","items":["The design should be tested using representative data.","Security and privacy should be considered from the start.","The chosen approach should be justified against relevant constraints.","Clear documentation makes a system easier to maintain.","The solution should meet the stated user need.","Inputs, processing and outputs should be identified clearly."]}]},"learning_guidance":{"hints":["For the wildlife centre’s computing systems, focus on computer science. Start from what the people using the system need it to achieve.","Connect the required result to its information, resources, checks and safeguards.","Weigh a benefit against a limitation for the wildlife centre’s computing systems, then decide which matters most to centre staff. Support the conclusion with those reasons."],"model_answer":"The design should be tested using representative data. This checks that the wildlife centre’s computing systems works for the kinds of input it is expected to receive.\\n\\nSecurity and privacy should be considered from the start. This helps avoid exposing information or allowing unauthorised actions in the wildlife centre’s computing systems.\\n\\nThe chosen approach should be justified against relevant constraints. For the wildlife centre’s computing systems, this means balancing user requirements against resources such as time, budget and available equipment.\\n\\nClear documentation makes a system easier to maintain. This helps another person operate, repair or extend the system supporting the wildlife centre’s computing systems.\\n\\nThe solution should meet the stated user need. For the wildlife centre’s computing systems, the organisation should establish what its users must be able to do before selecting technology.\\n\\nInputs, processing and outputs should be identified clearly. For the wildlife centre’s computing systems, this identifies what information enters the system, what it does with that information and what it returns.\\n\\nA useful design can improve the service, but extra features may increase cost, maintenance and privacy risks without helping the main user need.\\n\\nFor the wildlife centre’s computing systems, I would start with the core user need, choose a proportionate design and test its function, security and maintainability before expanding it. This balances the needs of centre staff against the limitatio