he fictional organisation:"},{"type":"list","items":["The solution should meet the stated user need.","Inputs, processing and outputs should be identified clearly.","The design should be tested using representative data.","Security and privacy should be considered from the start.","The chosen approach should be justified against relevant constraints.","Clear documentation makes a system easier to maintain."]}]},"learning_guidance":{"hints":["For the online booking service, focus on computer science. Start from what the people using the system need it to achieve.","Connect the required result to its information, resources, checks and safeguards.","Weigh a benefit against a limitation for the online booking service, then decide which matters most to booking-service users. Support the conclusion with those reasons."],"model_answer":"The solution should meet the stated user need. For the online booking service, the organisation should establish what its users must be able to do before selecting technology.\\n\\nInputs, processing and outputs should be identified clearly. For the online booking service, this identifies what information enters the system, what it does with that information and what it returns.\\n\\nThe design should be tested using representative data. This checks that the online booking service works for the kinds of input it is expected to receive.\\n\\nSecurity and privacy should be considered from the start. This helps avoid exposing information or allowing unauthorised actions in the online booking service.\\n\\nThe chosen approach should be justified against relevant constraints. For the online booking service, this means balancing user requirements against resources such as time, budget and available equipment.\\n\\nClear documentation makes a system easier to maintain. This helps another person operate, repair or extend the system supporting the online booking service.\\n\\nA useful design can improve the service, but extra features may increase cost, maintenance and privacy risks without helping the main user need.\\n\\nFor the online booking service, I would start with the core user need, choose a proportionate design and test its function, security and maintainability before expanding it. This balances the needs of booking-service users against the limitations above."}}]'),L_={paper_id:T_,qualification:C_,component:R_,title:S_,year:I_,session:P_,total_marks:O_,content_origin:j_,source_mode:E_,questions:F_},J_="J277-01-TeacherVariant-B",B_="J277",N_="01",D_="Computer Systems",H_=null,$_="TeacherVariant-B",V_=80,z_="comp-school-original-fixture",W_="original-fixture",U_=JSON.parse('[{"question_id":"1(a)","parent_question":1,"topic":"sound representation","marks":6,"command_word":"complete","content":[{"type":"text","value":"A local games studio is testing a prototype made with invented data. This is an original comp.school fixture scenario."},{"type":"text","value":"Complete 4 accurate points about sound representation."}],"answer":{"guidance":[{"type":"text","value":"Award marks for accurate, relevant points about sound representation; accept equivalent original wording."},{"type":"list","items":["A higher bit depth can represent amplitude more precisely but increases file size.","The duration of a recording also affects its file size.","Digital sound is created by measuring an analogue wave at regular intervals.","Sample rate is the number of samples taken per second.","Bit depth controls the number of amplitude values available for each sample.","A higher sample rate can improve fidelity but increases file size."]}],"marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"A higher bit depth can represent amplitude more precisely but increases file size.","marks":1},{"criteria":"The duration of a recording also affects its file size.","marks":1},{"criteria":"Digital sound is created by measuring an analogue wave at regular intervals.","marks":1},{"criteria":"Sample rate is the number of samples taken per second.","marks":1},{"cri