"]}]},"learning_guidance":{"hints":["For the online booking service, focus on computer science. Start from what the people using the system need it to achieve.","Connect the required result to its information, resources, checks and safeguards.","Weigh a benefit against a limitation for the online booking service, then decide which matters most to booking-service users. Support the conclusion with those reasons."],"model_answer":"Security and privacy should be considered from the start. This helps avoid exposing information or allowing unauthorised actions in the online booking service.\\n\\nThe chosen approach should be justified against relevant constraints. For the online booking service, this means balancing user requirements against resources such as time, budget and available equipment.\\n\\nClear documentation makes a system easier to maintain. This helps another person operate, repair or extend the system supporting the online booking service.\\n\\nThe solution should meet the stated user need. For the online booking service, the organisation should establish what its users must be able to do before selecting technology.\\n\\nInputs, processing and outputs should be identified clearly. For the online booking service, this identifies what information enters the system, what it does with that information and what it returns.\\n\\nThe design should be tested using representative data. This checks that the online booking service works for the kinds of input it is expected to receive.\\n\\nA useful design can improve the service, but extra features may increase cost, maintenance and privacy risks without helping the main user need.\\n\\nFor the online booking service, I would start with the core user need, choose a proportionate design and test its function, security and maintainability before expanding it. This balances the needs of booking-service users against the limitations above."}},{"question_id":"4(a)","parent_question":4,"topic":"LAN vs WAN","marks":2,"co