etwork connects devices across a larger geographical area.","marks":1},{"criteria":"A switch forwards frames to the intended device on a local network.","marks":1},{"criteria":"A router forwards packets between different networks.","marks":1},{"criteria":"Client-server networks centralise services and administration.","marks":1}],"model_answer":[{"type":"text","value":"A strong response applies these computer networks ideas to the fictional organisation:"},{"type":"list","items":["Network performance is affected by bandwidth, latency, traffic and transmission media.","A local area network connects devices across a limited geographical area.","A wide area network connects devices across a larger geographical area.","A switch forwards frames to the intended device on a local network.","A router forwards packets between different networks.","Client-server networks centralise services and administration."]}]},"learning_guidance":{"hints":["For testing the games prototype, focus on computer networks. Identify which devices or locations need to exchange information.","Distinguish the scale of the connection, the equipment carrying data and the way shared services are managed.","Weigh a benefit against a limitation for testing the games prototype, then decide which matters most to the development team. Support the conclusion with those reasons."],"model_answer":"Network performance is affected by bandwidth, latency, traffic and transmission media. The organisation must consider both connection capacity and delay when planning data exchange for testing the games prototype.\\n\\nA local area network connects devices across a limited geographical area. This allows devices at one site to share resources used in testing the games prototype.\\n\\nA wide area network connects devices across a larger geographical area. This could connect the sites or remote services needed by testing the games prototype.\\n\\nA switch forwards frames to the intended device on a local network. This helps devices at the same site exchange data for testing the games prototype.\\n\\nA router forwards packets between different networks. This allows data for testing the games prototype to reach services outside the local network.\\n\\nClient-server networks centralise services and administration. This lets the organisation manage shared accounts and resources for testing the games prototype from a central service.\\n\\nSharing services can simplify administration, but network or server failures can interrupt access and the system needs access controls and maintenance.\\n\\nFor testing the games prototype, I would provide the connections and shared services actually needed, with enough capacity, appropriate access controls and a plan for service interruptions. This balances the needs of the development team against the limitations above."}},{"question_id":"9(a)","parent_question":9,"topic":"sound file size calculation","marks":2,"command_word":"calculate","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Oakfield Food Co-op is modernising its stock-control system. This is an original comp.school fixture scenario."},{"type":"text","value":"Work out a valid result for the sound representation task. Show each stage of the method clearly."}],"answer":{"guidance":[{"type":"text","value":"Award marks for accurate, relevant points about sound representation; accept equivalent original wording."},{"type":"list","items":["Bit depth controls the number of amplitude values available for each sample.","A higher sample rate can improve fidelity but increases file size."]}],"marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Bit depth controls the number of amplitude values available for each sample.","marks":1},{"criteria":"A higher sample rate can improve fidelity but increases file size.","marks":1}],"model_answer":[{"type":"text","value":"A strong response applies these sound representation ideas to the fictional organisation:"},{"type":"list","items":["Bit depth controls the number of amplitude values availa