olution should meet the stated user need.","Inputs, processing and outputs should be identified clearly.","The design should be tested using representative data.","Security and privacy should be considered from the start.","The chosen approach should be justified against relevant constraints."]}],"marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Clear documentation makes a system easier to maintain.","marks":1},{"criteria":"The solution should meet the stated user need.","marks":1},{"criteria":"Inputs, processing and outputs should be identified clearly.","marks":1},{"criteria":"The design should be tested using representative data.","marks":1},{"criteria":"Security and privacy should be considered from the start.","marks":1},{"criteria":"The chosen approach should be justified against relevant constraints.","marks":1}],"model_answer":[{"type":"text","value":"A strong response applies these computer science ideas to the fictional organisation:"},{"type":"list","items":["Clear documentation makes a system easier to maintain.","The solution should meet the stated user need.","Inputs, processing and outputs should be identified clearly.","The design should be tested using representative data.","Security and privacy should be considered from the start.","The chosen approach should be justified against relevant constraints."]}]},"learning_guidance":{"hints":["For data exchange between the bike-hire devices, focus on computer science. Start from what the people using the system need it to achieve.","Connect the required result to its information, resources, checks and safeguards.","Weigh a benefit against a limitation for data exchange between the bike-hire devices, then decide which matters most to bike-hire staff. Support the conclusion with those reasons."],"model_answer":"Clear documentation makes a system easier to maintain. This helps another person operate, repair or extend the system supporting data exchange between the bike-hire devices.\\n\\nThe solution should meet the stated user need. For data exchange between the bike-hire devices, the organisation should establish what its users must be able to do before selecting technology.\\n\\nInputs, processing and outputs should be identified clearly. For data exchange between the bike-hire devices, this identifies what information enters the system, what it does with that information and what it returns.\\n\\nThe design should be tested using representative data. This checks that data exchange between the bike-hire devices works for the kinds of input it is expected to receive.\\n\\nSecurity and privacy should be considered from the start. This helps avoid exposing information or allowing unauthorised actions in data exchange between the bike-hire devices.\\n\\nThe chosen approach should be justified against relevant constraints. For data exchange between the bike-hire devices, this means balancing user requirements against resources such as time, budget and available equipment.\\n\\nA useful design can improve the service, but extra features may increase cost, maintenance and privacy risks without helping the main user need.\\n\\nFor data exchange between the bike-hire devices, I would start with the core user need, choose a proportionate design and test its function, security and maintainability before expanding it. This balances the needs of bike-hire staff against the limitations above."}},{"question_id":"6(b)(ii)","parent_question":6,"topic":"star topology diagram","marks":3,"command_word":"draw","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Harbour Arts Centre is planning a new online booking service. This is an original comp.school fixture scenario."},{"type":"text","value":"Explain how primary memory is relevant to this situation. Link each point to the needs of the organisation."}],"answer":{"guidance":[{"type":"text","value":"Award marks for accurate, relevant points about primary memory; accept equivalent original wording."},{"type":"list","items":["More RAM can reduce the need to move data to slower secondary storage.","Virtual memory uses secondary storage when available RAM is insufficient.","Accessing virtual memory is slower than accessing RAM."]}],"marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"More RAM can reduce the need to move data to slower secondary storage.","marks":1},{"criteria":"Virtual memory uses secondary storage when available RAM is insufficient.","marks":1},{"criteria":"Accessing virtual memory is slower than accessing RAM.","marks":1}],"model_answer":[{"type":"text","value":"A strong response applies these primary memory ideas to the fictional organisation:"},{"type":"list","items":["More RAM can reduce the need to move data to slower secondary storage.","Virtual memory uses secondary storage when available RAM is insufficient.","Accessing virtual memory is slower than accessing RAM."]}]},"learning_guidance":{"hints":["For the online booking service, focus on primary memory. Think about what must be available while a device is running and what is needed when it starts.","Compare how long information must be kept with how quickly the running program needs it.","Link each technical point to an effect on the online booking service. Make the reason for that effect explicit, without assuming facts about the organisation that the scenario does not give."],"model_answer":"More RAM can reduce the need to move data to slower secondary storage. This can help the online booking service remain responsive when several programs are open.\\n\\nVirtual memory uses secondary storage when available RAM is insufficient. This lets the online booking service continue when RAM is full, although access to the displaced data is slower.\\n\\nAccessing virtual memory is slower than accessing RAM. Frequent use of virtual memory can therefore delay the online booking service."}},{"question_id":"6(c)","parent_question":6,"topic":"network security table","marks":6,"command_word":"complete","content":[{"type":"text","value":"A local games studio is testing a prototype made with invented data. This is an original comp.school fixture scenario."},{"type":"text","value":"Complete 4 accurate points about computer networks."}],"answer":{"guidance":[{"type":"text","value":"Award marks for accurate, relevant points about computer networks; accept equivalent original wording."},{"type":"list","items":["Network performance is affected by bandwidth, latency, traffic and transmission media.","A local area network connects devices across a limited geographical area.","A wide area network connects devices across a larger geographical area.","A switch forwards frames to the intended device on a local network.","A router forwards packets between different networks.","Client-server networks centralise services and administration."]}],"marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Network performance is affected by bandwidth, latency, traffic and transmission media.","marks":1},{"criteria":"A local area network connects devices across a limited geographical area.","marks":1},{"criteria":"A wide area network connects devices across a larger geographical area.","marks":1},{"criteria":"A switch forwards frames to the intended device on a local network.","marks":1},{"criteria":"A router forwards packets between different networks.","marks":1},{"criteria":"Client-server networks centralise services and administration.","marks":1}],"model_answer":[{"type":"text","value":"A strong response applies these computer networks ideas to the fictional organisation:"},{"type":"list","items":["Network performance is affected by bandwidth, latency, traffic and transmission media.","A local area network connects devices across a limited geographical area.","A wide area network connects devices across a larger geographical area.","A switch forwards frames to the intended device on a local network.","A router forwards packets between different networks.","Client-server networks centralise services and administration."]}]},"learning_guidance":{"hints":["For testing the games prototype, focus on computer networks. Identify which devices or locations need to exchange information.","Distinguish the scale of the connection, the equipment carrying data and the way shared services are managed.","For each of your 4 points, explain why the property matters to testing the games prototype. Link related details where useful, and make the reason explicit rather than only naming a feature."],"model_answer":"- Network performance is affected by bandwidth, latency, traffic and transmission media. The organisation must consider both connection capacity and delay when planning data exchange for testing the games prototype.\\n- A local area network connects devices across a limited geographical area. This allows devices at one site to share resources used in testing the games prototype. A wide area network connects devices across a larger geographical area. This could connect the sites or remote services needed by testing the games prototype.\\n- A switch forwards frames to the intended device on a local network. This helps devices at the same site exchange data for testing the games prototype. A router forwards packets between different networks. This allows data for testing the games prototype to reach services outside the local network.\\n- Client-server networks centralise services and administration. This lets the organisation manage shared accounts and resources for testing the games prototype from a central service."}},{"question_id":"7(a)","parent_question":7,"topic":"defragmentation benefits","marks":3,"command_word":"explain","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Oakfield Food Co-op is modernising its stock-control system. This is an original comp.school fixture scenario."},{"type":"text","value":"Explain how systems software is relevant to this situation. Link each point to the needs of the organisation."}],"answer":{"guidance":[{"type":"text","value":"Award marks for accurate, relevant points about systems software; accept equivalent original wording."},{"type":"list","items":["File management organises stored files and folders.","User management applies accounts and permissions.","Backup utilities create recoverable copies of data."]}],"marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"File management organises stored files and folders.","marks":1},{"criteria":"User management applies accounts and permissions.","marks":1},{"criteria":"Backup utilities create recoverable copies of data.","marks":1}],"model_answer":[{"type":"text","value":"A strong response applies these systems software ideas to the fictional organisation:"},{"type":"list","items":["File management organises stored files and folders.","User management applies accounts and permissions.","Backup utilities create recoverable copies of data."]}]},"learning_guidance":{"hints":["For the stock-control system, focus on systems software. Think about the work needed to make hardware and applications usable.","Separate the management of running resources, stored files, user access and recovery.","Link each technical point to an effect on the stock-control system. Make the reason for that effect explicit, without assuming facts about the organisation that the scenario does not give."],"model_answer":"File management organises stored files and folders. This helps the organisation find and update the records used in the stock-control system.\\n\\nUser management applies accounts and permissions. This lets the organisation restrict access to the tools and records needed for the stock-control system.\\n\\nBackup utilities create recoverable copies of data. This provides a way to restore the data needed for the stock-control system after loss or damage."}},{"question_id":"7(b)","parent_question":7,"topic":"OS function categories","marks":5,"command_word":"tick","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Northbridge Community Library is improving its digital services. This is an original comp.school fixture scenario."},{"type":"text","value":"Tick 4 accurate points about programming fundamentals."}],"answer":{"guidance":[{"type":"text","value":"Award marks for accurate, relevant points about programming fundamentals; accept equivalent original wording."},{"type":"list","items":["Validation checks whether input is sensible before it is processed.","Variables store values that can change while a program runs.","Selection chooses which statements run according to a condition.","Iteration repeats statements while a condition holds or for a known number of times.","Arrays store multiple related values under one identifier."]}],"marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Validation checks whether input is sensible before it is processed.","marks":1},{"criteria":"Variables store values that can change while a program runs.","marks":1},{"criteria":"Selection chooses which statements run according to a condition.","marks":1},{"criteria":"Iteration repeats statements while a condition holds or for a known number of times.","marks":1},{"criteria":"Arrays store multiple related values under one identifier.","marks":1}],"model_answer":[{"type":"text","value":"A strong response applies these programming fundamentals ideas to the fictional organisation:"},{"type":"list","items":["Validation checks whether input is sensible before it is processed.","Variables store values that can change while a program runs.","Selection chooses which statements run according to a condition.","Iteration repeats statements while a condition holds or for a known number of times.","Arrays store multiple related values under one identifier."]}]},"learning_guidance":{"hints":["For the library’s digital services, focus on programming fundamentals. Think about the values the program needs and how its behaviour changes as it runs.","Trace where a value is stored, where a decision is made and where processing may repeat.","For each of your 4 points, explain why the property matters to the library’s digital services. Link related details where useful, and make the reason explicit rather than only naming a feature."],"model_answer":"- Validation checks whether input is sensible before it is processed. This helps prevent unsuitable input from causing incorrect processing in the library’s digital services.\\n- Variables store values that can change while a program runs. This lets the software for the library’s digital services update values as new input arrives.\\n- Selection chooses which statements run according to a condition. This lets the software for the library’s digital services respond differently to different inputs. Iteration repeats statements while a condition holds or for a known number of times. This allows repeated processing in the library’s digital services without writing the same statements many times.\\n- Arrays store multiple related values under one identifier. This allows related records used in the library’s digital services to be accessed by position in one collection."}},{"question_id":"7(c)(i)","parent_question":7,"topic":"open source benefits","marks":2,"command_word":"give","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Riverside Wildlife Centre is updating its computing systems. This is an original comp.school fixture scenario."},{"type":"text","value":"Give 2 accurate points about computer science."}],"answer":{"guidance":[{"type":"text","value":"Award marks for accurate, relevant points about computer science; accept equivalent original wording."},{"type":"list","items":["The design should be tested using representative data.","Security and privacy should be considered from the start."]}],"marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"The design should be tested using representative data.","marks":1},{"criteria":"Security and privacy should be considered from the start.","marks":1}],"model_answer":[{"type":"text","value":"A strong response applies these computer science ideas to the fictional organisation:"},{"type":"list","items":["The design should be tested using representative data.","Security and privacy should be considered from the start."]}]},"learning_guidance":{"hi