:["Backups should be stored separately from the original data.","Secondary storage retains data when power is removed.","Solid-state storage has no moving parts and usually provides fast access."]}]},"learning_guidance":{"hints":["For the online booking service, focus on secondary storage. Consider the files that must still exist after the device is switched off.","Compare the demands of keeping a large collection, accessing it quickly and protecting it from loss.","Link each technical point to an effect on the online booking service. Make the reason for that effect explicit, without assuming facts about the organisation that the scenario does not give."],"model_answer":"Backups should be stored separately from the original data. A separate copy allows the organisation to recover the records for the online booking service if its main storage fails.\\n\\nSecondary storage retains data when power is removed. This allows the records used in the online booking service to survive a shutdown.\\n\\nSolid-state storage has no moving parts and usually provides fast access. This can make loading data for the online booking service faster and avoids damage to moving storage parts."}}]'),XA={paper_id:DA,qualification:HA,component:$A,title:VA,year:zA,session:WA,total_marks:UA,content_origin:GA,source_mode:YA,questions:KA},QA="J277-01-2022-June",ZA="J277",e1="01",t1="Computer Systems",a1=2022,i1="June",s1=80,r1="comp-school-original-fixture",n1="original-fixture",o1=JSON.parse('[{"question_id":"1(a)","parent_question":1,"topic":"binary unit equivalents","marks":4,"command_word":"identify","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Greenway Bike Hire is reviewing how its devices exchange data. This is an original comp.school fixture scenario."},{"type":"text","value":"Identify 4 accurate points about number representation."}],"answer":{"guidance":[{"type":"text","value":"Award marks for accurate, relevant points about number representation; accept equivalent original wording."},{"type":"l