attacks.","marks":1},{"criteria":"Regular updates remove known vulnerabilities from software.","marks":1}],"model_answer":[{"type":"text","value":"A strong response applies these network security ideas to the fictional organisation:"},{"type":"list","items":["Authentication checks that a user is who they claim to be.","Access control limits users to the data and actions they need.","A firewall filters network traffic using configured rules.","Anti-malware software detects and removes known malicious software.","Staff training can reduce the success of social-engineering attacks.","Regular updates remove known vulnerabilities from software."]}]},"learning_guidance":{"hints":["For the stock-control system, focus on network security. Identify who should be able to use the system and which information needs protection.","Consider how an unwanted action could enter the system and where a safeguard could interrupt it.","For each of your 4 points, explain why the property matters to the stock-control system. Link related details where useful, and make the reason explicit rather than only naming a feature."],"model_answer":"- Authentication checks that a user is who they claim to be. This helps prevent an unauthorised person from using another person’s account in the stock-control system. Access control limits users to the data and actions they need. This reduces unnecessary access to the records and controls used in the stock-control system.\\n- A firewall filters network traffic using configured rules. This can block unwanted connections to systems supporting the stock-control system.\\n- Anti-malware software detects and removes known malicious software. This reduces the risk that malicious software disrupts the stock-control system or damages its data. Regular updates remove known vulnerabilities from software. Patching the systems used in the stock-control system reduces exposure to already identified weaknesses.\\n- Staff training can reduce the success of social-engi