 be useful for distributing or archiving modest amounts of data.","marks":1},{"criteria":"Capacity, speed, durability, portability and cost affect the choice of storage.","marks":1}],"model_answer":[{"type":"text","value":"A strong response applies these secondary storage ideas to the fictional organisation:"},{"type":"list","items":["Solid-state storage has no moving parts and usually provides fast access.","Magnetic storage can provide high capacity at a relatively low cost.","Optical media can be useful for distributing or archiving modest amounts of data.","Capacity, speed, durability, portability and cost affect the choice of storage."]}]},"learning_guidance":{"hints":["For the stock-control system, focus on secondary storage. Consider the files that must still exist after the device is switched off.","Compare the demands of keeping a large collection, accessing it quickly and protecting it from loss.","Link each technical point to an effect on the stock-control system. Make the reason for that effect explicit, without assuming facts about the organisation that the scenario does not give."],"model_answer":"Solid-state storage has no moving parts and usually provides fast access. This can make loading data for the stock-control system faster and avoids damage to moving storage parts.\\n\\nMagnetic storage can provide high capacity at a relatively low cost. This can make storing a large collection of records for the stock-control system more affordable.\\n\\nOptical media can be useful for distributing or archiving modest amounts of data. This could provide an offline distribution or archive copy for the stock-control system, if suitable drives are available.\\n\\nCapacity, speed, durability, portability and cost affect the choice of storage. The storage used for the stock-control system must balance the amount of data, access needs and available budget."}},{"question_id":"10(d)","parent_question":10,"topic":"legislation identification","marks":6,"command_word":"