ffected by bandwidth, latency, traffic and transmission media.","marks":1},{"criteria":"A local area network connects devices across a limited geographical area.","marks":1},{"criteria":"A wide area network connects devices across a larger geographical area.","marks":1}],"model_answer":[{"type":"text","value":"A strong response applies these computer networks ideas to the fictional organisation:"},{"type":"list","items":["Client-server networks centralise services and administration.","Network performance is affected by bandwidth, latency, traffic and transmission media.","A local area network connects devices across a limited geographical area.","A wide area network connects devices across a larger geographical area."]}]},"learning_guidance":{"hints":["For testing the games prototype, focus on computer networks. Identify which devices or locations need to exchange information.","Distinguish the scale of the connection, the equipment carrying data and the way shared services are managed.","Link each technical point to an effect on testing the games prototype. Make the reason for that effect explicit, without assuming facts about the organisation that the scenario does not give."],"model_answer":"Client-server networks centralise services and administration. This lets the organisation manage shared accounts and resources for testing the games prototype from a central service.\\n\\nNetwork performance is affected by bandwidth, latency, traffic and transmission media. The organisation must consider both connection capacity and delay when planning data exchange for testing the games prototype.\\n\\nA local area network connects devices across a limited geographical area. This allows devices at one site to share resources used in testing the games prototype.\\n\\nA wide area network connects devices across a larger geographical area. This could connect the sites or remote services needed by testing the games prototype."}},{"question_id":"1(c)","parent_question":1,"topic":"cloud storage drawbacks","marks":5,"command_word":"describe","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Hilltop Health Trackers is evaluating a fictional wearable device. This is an original comp.school fixture scenario for topic 1.3.1."},{"type":"text","value":"Explain how secondary storage is relevant to this situation. Link each point to the needs of the organisation."}],"answer":{"guidance":[{"type":"text","value":"Award marks for accurate, relevant points about secondary storage; accept equivalent original wording."},{"type":"list","items":["Solid-state storage has no moving parts and usually provides fast access.","Magnetic storage can provide high capacity at a relatively low cost.","Optical media can be useful for distributing or archiving modest amounts of data.","Capacity, speed, durability, portability and cost affect the choice of storage.","Backups should be stored separately from the original data."]}],"marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Solid-state storage has no moving parts and usually provides fast access.","marks":1},{"criteria":"Magnetic storage can provide high capacity at a relatively low cost.","marks":1},{"criteria":"Optical media can be useful for distributing or archiving modest amounts of data.","marks":1},{"criteria":"Capacity, speed, durability, portability and cost affect the choice of storage.","marks":1},{"criteria":"Backups should be stored separately from the original data.","marks":1}],"model_answer":[{"type":"text","value":"A strong response applies these secondary storage ideas to the fictional organisation:"},{"type":"list","items":["Solid-state storage has no moving parts and usually provides fast access.","Magnetic storage can provide high capacity at a relatively low cost.","Optical media can be useful for distributing or archiving modest amounts of data.","Capacity, speed, durability, portability and cost affect the choice of storage.","Backups should be stored separately from the original data."]}]},"learning_guidance":{"hints":["For